# Build context for the BACKEND image, whose context is this directory (the repo
# root) rather than ./backend — it has to reach supabase/migrations and
# forge-growth-plugin, and Docker cannot COPY from a parent of its context.
#
# ⚠ THE FIRST ENTRY IS THE LOAD-BEARING ONE. A real .env lives here on any
# machine that has run ./scripts/install.sh, and a root build context would
# otherwise upload every secret in it to the daemon. The COPY lines in
# backend/Dockerfile are specific, so nothing lands in the published image
# today — but one broad `COPY . .` added later would publish the lot. Excluding
# it here means that mistake cannot become a leak.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Never needed in an image, and the single biggest cause of a slow build: the
# daemon tars the whole context before the first instruction runs.
**/node_modules
.git
.github

# Frontend sources — the backend image does not build the UI. Its own image has
# its own context (./frontend) and therefore its own .dockerignore.
frontend

# Local artefacts
**/dist
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/coverage
uploads
media
